Package: msomgom
Title: Multi-Species Occupancy Model of the Gulf of Maine
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Camille", "Ross", email = "camille.ross@maine.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fits a dynamic (multi-season, colonization/persistence) occupancy
    model, following MacKenzie et al. (2003) <doi:10.1890/02-3090>, to
    cetacean vessel-survey sightings via JAGS. Config-driven data cleaning,
    spatial gridding, model fitting, and convergence evaluation, with optional
    environmental covariates on occupancy, persistence, and colonization built
    from Copernicus Marine Service data (e.g. via the 'datamatch' package,
    <https://github.com/chross22/datamatch>) or local NetCDF files. Originally
    built around Bay of Fundy North Atlantic right whale survey data from the
    NARWC Sightings Database, generalized so study area, date range, species,
    and MCMC settings are all config-driven rather than hardcoded.
